==English==
{{was wotd|2025|April|16}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|id=before|*weyd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|prudence|t=discretion; foresight; knowledge; intelligence, wisdom; act of good judgment; wisdom to see what is virtuous}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=prūdence|pos=n|id=MED35090|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|prudence}}, {{der|en|frm|prudence}}, and {{der|en|fro|prudence|t=common sense; wisdom}} (modern {{cog|fr|prudence}}), and from their {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|prūdentia|t=common sense; discretion, prudence; foresight; knowledge; providence; skilfulness; wisdom}}, from ''prūdent-'' (the {{glossary|stem}} of {{m|la|prūdēns|t=knowledgeable, skilful; wise, prudent}}) + {{m|la|-ia|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming first-{{glossary|declension}} {{glossary|feminine}} {{glossary|abstract noun}}s}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=4479669186|date=December 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> {{m|la||Prūdēns}} is a {{glossary|contraction}} of {{m|la|prōvidēns|t=caring for; foreseeing; providing}} (whence {{m|la|prōvidentia|t=foreknowledge, foresight; forethought, precaution, providence}}), the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|prōvideō|t=to care for, look after; to foresee; to provide, see to}}, from {{m|la|prō-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘forward; prior’}} + {{m|la|videō|t=to perceive, see; to comprehend, understand; to look out for, care for}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*weyd-|t=to see; to know}}). {{doublet|en|provide|purvey}}.

